  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Airport Management and Operations Efficiency Training Program FAA Transfer Funds, through U.S. Government - Department of Transportation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USTDA funding will enable the U.S. Federal Aviation Administration to provide subject matter experts to participate in the Airport Mangement and Operations Efficiency Training Program (AMOETP) technical assistance. The Grantee for this activity is the Civil Aviation Administration of China, and the American Chamber of Commerce in China Fund serves as the sole-source Contractor, on behalf of the U.S.-China Aviation Cooperation Program. The purpose of this training program is to improve the operations and management of Chinese airports to ensure that, as China&apos;s air traffic grows, air travel remains safe and efficient, and to support opportunities for U.S. suppliers of airport-related goods, services and technologies to participate in the development of China&apos;s airports.</narrative>
  </description>
